{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 6}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   This document specifies version 1.3 of the Datagram Transport Layer\n   Security (DTLS) protocol.  DTLS 1.3 allows client/server applications\n   to communicate over the Internet in a way that is designed to prevent\n   eavesdropping, tampering, and message forgery.\n\n   The DTLS 1.3 protocol is based on the Transport Layer Security (TLS)\n   1.3 protocol and provides equivalent security guarantees with the\n   exception of order protection / non-replayability.  Datagram\n   semantics of the underlying transport are preserved by the DTLS\n   protocol.\n\n   This document obsoletes RFC 6347.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc9147bis/", "expires": "2025-06-17T16:27:46Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 379771, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc9147bis", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 69, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/379771/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2024-12-14T16:27:46Z", "title": "The Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) Protocol Version 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies version 1.3 of the Datagram Transport Layer\n   Security (DTLS) protocol.  DTLS 1.3 allows client/server applications\n   to communicate over the Internet in a way that is designed to prevent\n   eavesdropping, tampering, and message forgery.\n\n   The DTLS 1.3 protocol is based on the Transport Layer Security (TLS)\n   1.3 protocol and provides equivalent security guarantees with the\n   exception of order protection / non-replayability.  Datagram\n   semantics of the underlying transport are preserved by the DTLS\n   protocol.\n\n   This document obsoletes RFC 6347.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc9147bis/", "expires": "2025-06-17T16:27:46Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 383144, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc9147bis", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 69, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/383144/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2025-02-10T21:15:19Z", "title": "The Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) Protocol Version 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies version 1.3 of the Datagram Transport Layer\n   Security (DTLS) protocol.  DTLS 1.3 allows client/server applications\n   to communicate over the Internet in a way that is designed to prevent\n   eavesdropping, tampering, and message forgery.\n\n   The DTLS 1.3 protocol is based on the Transport Layer Security (TLS)\n   1.3 protocol and provides equivalent security guarantees with the\n   exception of order protection / non-replayability.  Datagram\n   semantics of the underlying transport are preserved by the DTLS\n   protocol.\n\n   This document obsoletes RFC 6347.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-rfc9147bis/", "expires": "2025-06-17T16:27:46Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 393915, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-rfc9147bis", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 69, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/393915/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/